        <h3>Data Processing Agreement</h3>
        <p>We have concluded a data processing agreement (DPA) for the use of the above-mentioned service[cite: 10]. This is a contract required by data protection law, which ensures that the provider processes the personal data of our website visitors only in accordance with our instructions and in compliance with the GDPR[cite: 10].</p>

        <h2>3. General Notes and Required Information</h2>
        <h3>Data Protection</h3>
        <p>The operators of these pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously[cite: 10]. We treat your personal data confidentially and in accordance with the statutory data protection regulations and this privacy policy[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>When you use this website, various personal data are collected[cite: 10]. Personal data is data with which you can be personally identified[cite: 10]. This privacy policy explains what data we collect and what we use it for[cite: 10]. It also explains how and for what purpose this happens[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>We point out that data transmission over the Internet (e.g., when communicating by email) can have security gaps[cite: 10]. A complete protection of data against access by third parties is not possible[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>Information on the Responsible Party</h3>
        <p>The responsible party for data processing on this website is:<br />
        <strong>Dante Joaquin Pino Suarez</strong><br />
        Ufnaustraße 16<br />
        10553 Berlin<br />
        Phone: 016096579389<br />
        Email: pinosuarezjoaquin@gmail.com[cite: 10]</p>
        <p>The responsible party is the natural or legal person who alone or jointly with others decides on the purposes and means of processing personal data (e.g., names, email addresses, etc.)[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>Storage Period</h3>
        <p>Unless a more specific storage period has been specified within this privacy policy, your personal data will remain with us until the purpose for data processing no longer applies[cite: 10]. If you assert a legitimate request for deletion or revoke your consent to data processing, your data will be deleted unless we have other legally permissible reasons for storing your personal data (e.g., tax or commercial law retention periods); in the latter case, deletion takes place after these reasons no longer apply[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>General Notes on the Legal Basis for Data Processing on this Website</h3>
        <p>If you have consented to data processing, we process your personal data on the basis of Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. a GDPR or Art. 9 Abs. 2 lit. a GDPR if special categories of data according to Art. 9 Abs. 1 GDPR are processed[cite: 10]. In the case of explicit consent to the transfer of personal data to third countries, data processing is also based on Art. 49 Abs. 1 lit. a GDPR[cite: 10]. If you have consented to the storage of cookies or to access to information in your terminal device (e.g., via device fingerprinting), data processing is additionally based on § 25 Abs. 1 TDDDG[cite: 10]. Consent can be revoked at any time[cite: 10]. If your data is required for contract fulfillment or to carry out pre-contractual measures, we process your data on the basis of Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. b GDPR[cite: 10]. Furthermore, we process your data if it is required to fulfill a legal obligation on the basis of Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. c GDPR[cite: 10]. Data processing can also take place on the basis of our legitimate interest according to Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. f GDPR[cite: 10]. Information about the legal basis applicable in each individual case is provided in the following paragraphs of this privacy policy[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>Recipients of Personal Data</h3>
        <p>As part of our business activities, we work with various external bodies[cite: 10]. In some cases, a transfer of personal data to these external bodies is also necessary[cite: 10]. We only pass on personal data to external bodies if this is necessary within the framework of contract fulfillment, if we are legally obliged to do so (e.g., passing on data to tax authorities), if we have a legitimate interest according to Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. f GDPR in passing it on, or if another legal basis permits the data transfer[cite: 10]. When using processors, we only pass on personal data of our clients on the basis of a valid contract on data processing[cite: 10]. In the case of joint processing, a joint processing contract is concluded[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>Revocation of Your Consent to Data Processing</h3>
        <p>Many data processing operations are only possible with your express consent[cite: 10]. You can revoke consent you have already given at any time[cite: 10]. The legality of the data processing carried out up to the revocation remains unaffected by the revocation[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>Right to Object to Data Collection in Special Cases and to Direct Marketing (Art. 21 GDPR)</h3>
        <p>IF DATA PROCESSING IS BASED ON ART. 6 ABS. 1 LIT. E OR F GDPR, YOU HAVE THE RIGHT AT ANY TIME, FOR REASONS ARISING FROM YOUR PARTICULAR SITUATION, TO OBJECT TO THE PROCESSING OF YOUR PERSONAL DATA; THIS ALSO APPLIES TO PROFILING BASED ON THESE PROVISIONS[cite: 10]. THE RESPECTIVE LEGAL BASIS ON WHICH PROCESSING IS BASED CAN BE FOUND IN THIS PRIVACY POLICY[cite: 10]. IF YOU OBJECT, WE WILL NO LONGER PROCESS YOUR AFFECTED PERSONAL DATA UNLESS WE CAN DEMONSTRATE COMPELLING LEGITIMATE GROUNDS FOR PROCESSING WHICH OVERRIDE YOUR INTERESTS, RIGHTS, AND FREEDOMS, OR THE PROCESSING SERVES THE ESTABLISHMENT, EXERCISE, OR DEFENSE OF LEGAL CLAIMS (OBJECTION ACCORDING TO ART. 21 ABS. 1 GDPR)[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>IF YOUR PERSONAL DATA IS PROCESSED FOR THE PURPOSE OF DIRECT MARKETING, YOU HAVE THE RIGHT TO OBJECT AT ANY TIME TO THE PROCESSING OF PERSONAL DATA CONCERNING YOU FOR THE PURPOSE OF SUCH MARKETING; THIS ALSO APPLIES TO PROFILING INSOFAR AS IT IS CONNECTED WITH SUCH DIRECT MARKETING[cite: 10]. IF YOU OBJECT, YOUR PERSONAL DATA WILL SUBSEQUENTLY NO LONGER BE USED FOR THE PURPOSE OF DIRECT MARKETING (OBJECTION ACCORDING TO ART. 21 ABS. 2 GDPR)[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>Right to Lodge a Complaint with the Competent Supervisory Authority</h3>
        <p>In the event of violations of the GDPR, data subjects have a right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, in particular in the Member State of their habitual residence, their place of work, or the place of the alleged violation[cite: 10]. The right to lodge a complaint is without prejudice to any other administrative or judicial remedies[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>Right to Data Portability</h3>
        <p>You have the right to have data that we process automatically on the basis of your consent or in fulfillment of a contract handed over to you or to a third party in a common, machine-readable format[cite: 10]. If you request the direct transfer of data to another responsible party, this will only be done insofar as it is technically feasible[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>Information, Correction, and Deletion</h3>
        <p>Within the framework of the applicable statutory provisions, you have the right at any time to free information about your stored personal data, its origin and recipient, and the purpose of data processing and, if applicable, a right to correction or deletion of this data[cite: 10]. You can contact us at any time regarding this and other questions on the subject of personal data[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>Right to Restriction of Processing</h3>
        <p>You have the right to request the restriction of processing of your personal data[cite: 10]. You can contact us at any time regarding this[cite: 10]. The right to restriction of processing exists in the following cases:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>If you dispute the accuracy of your personal data stored with us, we usually need time to verify this[cite: 10]. For the duration of the audit, you have the right to request the restriction of the processing of your personal data[cite: 10].</li>
          <li>If the processing of your personal data happened/happens unlawfully, you can request the restriction of data processing instead of deletion[cite: 10].</li>
          <li>If we no longer need your personal data, but you need it to exercise, defend, or assert legal claims, you have the right to request the restriction of processing of your personal data instead of deletion[cite: 10].</li>
          <li>If you have lodged an objection pursuant to Art. 21 Abs. 1 GDPR, a balance must be struck between your interests and ours[cite: 10]. As long as it is not yet clear whose interests prevail, you have the right to request the restriction of the processing of your personal data[cite: 10].</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you have restricted the processing of your personal data, this data – apart from its storage – may only be processed with your consent or for the establishment, exercise, or defense of legal claims or for the protection of the rights of another natural or legal person or for reasons of important public interest of the European Union or a Member State[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>SSL or TLS Encryption</h3>
        <p>This site uses SSL or TLS encryption for security reasons and to protect the transmission of confidential content, such as orders or inquiries that you send to us as the site operator[cite: 10]. You can recognize an encrypted connection by the fact that the address line of the browser changes from "http://" to "https://" and by the lock symbol in your browser line[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>If SSL or TLS encryption is activated, the data you transmit to us cannot be read by third parties[cite: 10].</p>

        <h2>4. Data Collection on This Website</h2>
        <h3>Cookies</h3>
        <p>Our internet pages use so-called "cookies"[cite: 10]. Cookies are small data packets and do not cause any damage to your terminal device[cite: 10]. They are stored either temporarily for the duration of a session (session cookies) or permanently (permanent cookies) on your terminal device[cite: 10]. Session cookies are automatically deleted at the end of your visit[cite: 10]. Permanent cookies remain stored on your terminal device until you delete them yourself or an automatic deletion is carried out by your web browser[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>Cookies can come from us (first-party cookies) or from third-party companies (so-called third-party cookies)[cite: 10]. Third-party cookies enable the integration of certain services from third-party companies within websites (e.g., cookies for processing payment services)[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>Cookies have various functions[cite: 10]. Numerous cookies are technically necessary, as certain website functions would not work without them (e.g., the shopping cart function or the display of videos)[cite: 10]. Other cookies can be used to evaluate user behavior or for advertising purposes[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>Cookies that are required to carry out the electronic communication process, to provide certain functions desired by you (e.g., for the shopping cart function) or to optimize the website (e.g., cookies to measure the web audience) (necessary cookies) are stored on the basis of Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. f GDPR unless another legal basis is specified[cite: 10]. The website operator has a legitimate interest in storing necessary cookies for the technically error-free and optimized provision of their services[cite: 10]. If consent to the storage of cookies and comparable recognition technologies has been requested, processing takes place exclusively on the basis of this consent (Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. a GDPR and § 25 Abs. 1 TDDDG); the consent can be revoked at any time[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>You can set your browser so that you are informed about the setting of cookies and allow cookies only in individual cases, exclude the acceptance of cookies for certain cases or in general, and activate the automatic deletion of cookies when closing the browser[cite: 10]. If cookies are deactivated, the functionality of this website may be limited[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>Contact Form</h3>
        <p>If you send us inquiries via the contact form, your details from the inquiry form, including the contact details you provided there, will be stored by us for the purpose of processing the inquiry and in the case of follow-up questions[cite: 10]. We do not pass on this data without your consent[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>The processing of this data is based on Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. b GDPR if your inquiry is related to the fulfillment of a contract or is necessary to carry out pre-contractual measures[cite: 10]. In all other cases, processing is based on our legitimate interest in the effective processing of inquiries addressed to us (Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. f GDPR) or on your consent (Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. a GDPR) if this was requested; the consent can be revoked at any time[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>The data you enter into the contact form will remain with us until you request us to delete it, revoke your consent to storage, or the purpose for data storage no longer applies (e.g., after your inquiry has been processed)[cite: 10]. Mandatory statutory provisions – in particular retention periods – remain unaffected[cite: 10].</p>

        <h3>Inquiry by Email, Phone, or Fax</h3>
        <p>If you contact us by email, phone, or fax, your inquiry, including all personal data resulting from it (name, inquiry), will be stored and processed by us for the purpose of processing your request[cite: 10]. We do not pass on this data without your consent[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>The processing of this data is based on Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. b GDPR if your inquiry is related to the fulfillment of a contract or is necessary to carry out pre-contractual measures[cite: 10]. In all other cases, processing is based on our legitimate interest in the effective processing of inquiries addressed to us (Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. f GDPR) or on your consent (Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. a GDPR) if this was requested; the consent can be revoked at any time[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>The data you send to us via contact inquiries will remain with us until you request us to delete it, revoke your consent to storage, or the purpose for data storage no longer applies (e.g., after your request has been processed)[cite: 10]. Mandatory statutory provisions – in particular statutory retention periods – remain unaffected[cite: 10].</p>

        <h2>5. Plugins and Tools</h2>
        <h3>Google Fonts (Local Hosting)</h3>
        <p>This site uses so-called Google Fonts, provided by Google, for the uniform display of fonts[cite: 10]. The Google Fonts are installed locally[cite: 10]. A connection to Google servers does not take place[cite: 10].</p>
        <p>Further information about Google Fonts can be found at <a href="https://developers.google.com/fonts/faq" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://developers.google.com/fonts/faq</a> and in Google's privacy policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en</a>[cite: 10].</p>
